Keybindings of the Omarchy desktop (niri). Super is the Windows or Command key.
The configuration is ~/.config/niri/config.kdl; niri reloads it when it changes.

Windows and workspaces
  Super+Return            terminal (foot)
  Super+Space             launcher (fuzzel): type the name of an app
  Super+Alt+Space         the menu: install, update, lock, restart, shut down
  Super+W                 close the window (also Super+Shift+Q)
  Super+H J K L           focus left, down, up, right (or the arrow keys)
  Super+Shift+H J K L     move the column or the window (or the arrow keys)
  Super+Ctrl+Left Right   the column's width, narrower or wider
  Super+Ctrl+Up Down      the window's height, shorter or taller
  Super+R                 the column's width: the next preset (a third, half, two thirds)
  Super+1 .. 0            workspace 1 .. 10
  Super+Shift+1 .. 0      move the window to workspace 1 .. 10
  Super+Tab               the previous workspace
  Super+F                 fullscreen
  Super+T                 floating or tiled
  Super+S                 the column's windows in tabs (again: back to a column)

Screen and notifications
  Print                   screenshot of the whole screen to ~/Pictures and the clipboard
  Super+Shift+S           screenshot of a region (drag with the mouse)
  Super+N                 dismiss the notification
  Super+Escape            lock the screen (Super+Ctrl+L too); needs a password: sudo passwd user

Desktop
  Super+Shift+/           the keys of niri itself (the hotkey overlay)
  Super+Shift+E           exit the desktop (niri asks first)

Terminal (foot)
  Ctrl+Shift+C / V        copy and paste
  Ctrl+Shift+R            search the scrollback
  Shift+Page Up / Down    scroll by page (the mouse wheel works too)

Shell (bash)
  Ctrl+R                  search the history (fzf)
  Ctrl+T                  insert a file name (fzf)
  Alt+C                   change to a directory (fzf)
  z NAME                  jump to a directory you have used (zoxide)
  v, lg, top              neovim, lazygit, btop

tmux (ctrl-a is the prefix)
  prefix |  /  prefix -   split the window to the right or below
  prefix c                new window
  prefix d                detach

Neovim (Space is the leader)
  Space w, Space q        save, quit
  Space f f               find a file below the directory (:find)
  Space f b               list the buffers
  Space e                 the file browser (netrw)
  Ctrl+h J K L            move between windows
